COMPILATION OF: E49H5

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49H5

   1 a 0000 E49H5:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] `na > rec.s2' -- the BARE-LEFT twin of E49F2
   4 a 0006      (unequal extents 3/2, swapped, strict). H-B-invis predicts the
   5 a 0006      F2 golden's head exactly: swapped loads s2 first, positional
   6 a 0006      `06 02 / 3E 03' on the LOWERED operands, JNC d2, two
   7 a 0006      immediates (no collapse at unequal lengths).  Any refusal or
   8 a 0006      byte drift falsifies [C344]-transfer for relations. */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  14 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   if na > rec.s2 then k = 1;
  16 c 001E   put list('K=', k);
  17 c 0040   stop;
  18 a 0043 end E49H5;

CODE SIZE = 0043
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
